==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|prioritise||British}}

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|priority|-ize}}. {{etydate|1967}} as U.S. government {{glossary|jargon}}, becoming more widespread through the 1970s and ’80s, but still denounced as {{w|officialese}} by purists into the 1990s.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/pɹaɪˈɒɹ.ə.taɪz/|[pɹaɪˈɒɹ.taɪz]|a=RP}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-prioritize.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/pɹaɪˈoɹ.ə.taɪz/|[pɹaɪˈoɹ.taɪz]|a=GA,CA}}
* {{IPA|en|/pɹɑeˈɔɹ.ə.tɑez/|a=AU}}
* {{IPA|en|/pɹaɪˈɒɹ.ə.taɪz/|[pɹɑe̯ˈɔ̟ɹətɑe̯z]|a=NZ}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[value]], do, or choose something first, or before other things.
#: {{ux|en|When I don't have time to buy everything at the store, I '''prioritize''' fresh fruit and vegetables over foods like rice or noodles.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=1999-03-24|author=w:National Transportation Safety Board|title=Aircraft Accident Report: Uncontrolled Descent and Collision with Terrain, USAir Flight 427, Boeing 737-300, N513AU, Near Aliquippa, Pennsylvania, September 8, 1994|chapter=1.18.10.2.3 1997 Through 1998—Information and Changes Disseminated by Boeing|url=https://www.ntsb.gov/investigations/AccidentReports/Reports/AAR9901.pdf|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220604160926/https://www.ntsb.gov/investigations/AccidentReports/Reports/AAR9901.pdf|archivedate=4 June 2022|accessdate=7 December 2022|pages=205–206|text=Boeing's article stressed '''prioritizing''' roll control during recovery from nose-down bank upsets unless the airplane was in a stall condition; if the airplane was stalled, Boeing recommended recovering from the stall before recovering from the upset. The article described the nose-down upset recovery technique as follows: "Reduce angle of attack. This unloads the wing, allows the airplane to accelerate, which reduces rudder deflection and improves lateral control ability. {{...}}"}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|author={{w|Andy Weir}}|title={{w|Artemis (novel)|Artemis}}|chapter=17|page=295-6|text=Loretta's already designing the next smelter. She has some improvements in mind. The new one will '''prioritize''' silicon extraction and—}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive}} To [[arrange]] or [[list]] a group of things in [[order]] of [[priority]] or [[importance]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[rank]] something as having high priority.

